From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 16:32:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] mlow: speed up the encoder for 32-bit ARM

On the HP TouchPad (ARMv7) the pure-Go MLow encoder does not keep up with the
60 ms frame budget, so the send loop drops frames and the far end hears
gaps. Profiling showed most of the time in values that never change and
in a few scalar inner loops:

- cache the FFT twiddle factors per (length, sign) instead of calling
  cos/sin on every transform, and build the LPC DCT tables once
- on GOARCH=arm with cgo, run the FFT, the CELP Toeplitz and MA filter
  kernels and the pitch cross-correlation in C built with
  -mfpu=neon -O3; every other build keeps the Go code through the
  *_fallback.go build tags

The mlow tests pass on amd64 with these changes.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
